id: pm-chdp87
title: "commitItemMutations cannot compensate a create that clears a collection: the explicit_unset suffix hides the apply marker, so a refused batch reports transaction_partial_mutation and keeps the create"
description: "Found while implementing pm-gh1713 (2026-11-14). A strict-preset importer must pass the --clear-* options (clearDeps, clearComments and the rest) to satisfy strict create's required repeatables. When the create runs inside commitItemMutations, buildHistoryMessage appends ' | explicit_unset=dependencies,comments,...' to the transaction's apply marker. compensateCreatedItem and isUpdateMarkerApplied match the marker by exact string equality, so they never recognise the step's own create. When a later row fails, compensation therefore throws transaction_partial_mutation ('cannot safely compensate incomplete step'), the batch surfaces an AggregateError, and the created item stays open. Reproduced with no deferrals and with close validation off: a create step with clearDeps plus a failing update row. The same create without clear options rolls back cleanly. Fix: treat the marker as a prefix followed by ' | ' (isStepMarkerMessage) everywhere a step marker is matched. Duplicate check: searched compensation explicit_unset marker partial mutation; pm-wb6ktl covers guard-judged compensation, not marker matching."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:sdk",importers,strict-preset,transactions
created_at: "2026-11-14T06:08:20.927Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T09:04:51.432Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-14T09:04:49.754Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-14T09:04:49.754Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "A commitItemMutations batch whose create step clears collections rolls back cleanly when a later row fails, with no transaction_partial_mutation; Marker matching accepts the explicit_unset suffix and nothing else; A spec reproduces the refusal and passes after the fix"
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "isStepMarkerMessage in src/sdk/item-transaction.ts matches a step marker exactly or as a prefix followed by ' | '. buildHistoryMessage appends the ' | explicit_unset=...' suffix, which compensateCreatedItem, isUpdateMarkerApplied and the ownership proof missed. Compensation closes now pass validateClose off: a rollback close completes no work, so strict evidence or deferral validation no longer refuses it."
expected_result: A refused batch rolls back its strict-mode creates cleanly
actual_result: "Verified by spec on a strict-preset tracker: a batch whose deferred, collection-clearing create is followed by a failing row reports only the row's error, and the created item is closed by compensation. The negative control fails without the fix."
